# text = The Committee ’s report notes that it is “ not aware of a case relating to a sitting MP which has involved such a sustained and pervasive breach of the House ’s rules on registration , declaration and paid advocacy ” and concludes that the second - longest suspension since 1947 was the correct sanction for such a grievous breach .
