# text_id = 1216
# text = Given that the Institute of Economic Affairs called this morning for a ban on the universal service obligation , for zonal pricing and for not making deliveries six days a week in the countryside , is it not true that , if this privatisation goes through , the only way to guarantee that the conditions in the Bill remain active will be to vote Labour at the next election ?
