# text = When the Thames tunnel scheme to deal with sewage in the Thames — the system built in the Victorian era by Bazalgette is no longer fit for purpose — was first proposed , the general cost was said to be between £ 1 billion and £ 2 billion , but everybody now accepts that , at 2011 prices , the Thames tunnel would cost £ 4.1 billion or more .
