# text_id = 1255
# text = Mark Twain once said that prophecy — or , in this case , economic forecasting — is “ a good line of business , but it is full of risks ” , and in respect of certain Governments it is sometimes said that statistics , and even forecasts , can be used in the same way as “ a drunken man uses lamp posts — for support rather than illumination .
