# text_id = 1308
# text = Following the comprehensive spending review last week , which included a drastic attack on local government funding , many local authorities will be worrying about whether they should spend £ 10,000 on a registration campaign , to make sure that as many people as possible are on the register , or whether they should spend the money on keeping a swimming pool open or on some other element of their services .
