# text_id = 1311
# text = There are 2.7 million people on the dole — the highest number for 17 years — representing a huge cost to the economy in benefit payments and lost tax , a huge cost to the individuals affected and their families , and a cost to their local communities , many of which , especially in the north , are all too aware of the long - term scarring effects of unemployment .
