# text_id = 1335
# text = The Government have quite rightly apologised whenever the state or those acting for the state fell short of the high standards we expect , but I cannot emphasise enough that events like Bloody Sunday are not the defining story of Operation Banner , and those who served can rightly be proud of the role they played in ultimately bringing Northern Ireland to the much improved place that it is today .
