# text_id = 1357
# text = It would be different if someone were found guilty of an offence here but , as I have said , the Titles Deprivation Act 1917 provides a clearer , more suitable model that does not risk bringing the proceedings of the House under the eyes of the courts , because it would be the title of the peerage itself — the honour — that was in question , not the proceedings .
