# text_id = 1359
# text = Some years ago , when I was chair of the joint departmental research ethics committee at the University of Stirling , we were faced with a situation where research programmes into smoking were being challenged by business , which was trying to get access through legal means to the original data that the academics had used , so that the tobacco companies could twist them for their own interests .
